From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: report the TP port on the copper 10G PHYs

genphy_c45_pma_read_abilities() does not set ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_TP_BIT,
causing ethtool to print empty "Supported ports: [ ]" on RTL826x copper
PHYs. Set ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_TP_BIT in rtl8261x_get_features() and
rtl826x_get_features().

Origin: archive/xr1710g-v1@e85677d284c0
Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -525,6 +525,10 @@ static int rtl8261x_get_features(struct
 	ret = genphy_c45_pma_read_abilities(phydev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+
+	/* C45 PMA abilities omit medium; RTL8261x are copper TP PHYs. */
+	linkmode_set_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_TP_BIT, phydev->supported);
+
 	/*
 	 * Supplement Multi-Gig speeds that may not be automatically detected
 	 * RTL8261X supports 2.5G/5G in addition to standard 10G
@@ -4012,6 +4016,9 @@ static int rtl826x_get_features(struct p
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* C45 PMA abilities omit medium; RTL826x are copper TP PHYs. */
+	linkmode_set_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_TP_BIT, phydev->supported);
+
 	/* not support 10M modes */
 	linkmode_clear_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_10baseT_Half_BIT,
 			   phydev->supported);
